        "id": "p49-q43-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\sin(150^\\circ-\\theta)=\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt3}{2}\\sin\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The sine rule gives $\\dfrac{10}{\\sin\\theta}=\\dfrac{5(1+\\sqrt3)}{\\sin(150^\\circ-\\theta)}$, hence $\\sin(150^\\circ-\\theta)=\\dfrac{1+\\sqrt3}{2}\\sin\\theta$.",
          "worked": "The angles in $\\triangle LPQ$ give\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle LPQ&=180^\\circ-30^\\circ-\\theta\\\\\\angle LPQ&=150^\\circ-\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\n\nBy the sine rule,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{10}{\\sin\\theta}&=\\frac{5(1+\\sqrt3)}{\\sin(150^\\circ-\\theta)}\\\\10\\sin(150^\\circ-\\theta)&=5(1+\\sqrt3)\\sin\\theta\\\\\\sin(150^\\circ-\\theta)&=\\frac{1+\\sqrt3}{2}\\sin\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p49-q43-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the bearing of the lighthouse from $P$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p49-q43-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "345^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p49-q43-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Expand the sine difference to find ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\theta=45^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; the lighthouse is then 15° west of north from ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "P",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Expand the relation from part (a).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin150^\\circ\\cos\\theta-\\cos150^\\circ\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{1+\\sqrt3}{2}\\sin\\theta\\\\\\frac12\\cos\\theta+\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{1+\\sqrt3}{2}\\sin\\theta\\\\\\cos\\theta+\\sqrt3\\sin\\theta&=(1+\\sqrt3)\\sin\\theta\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\sin\\theta\\\\\\tan\\theta&=1\\\\\\theta&=45^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\angle LPQ=150^\\circ-45^\\circ=105^\\circ$. Since $PQ$ points east, $PL$ is $105^\\circ-90^\\circ=15^\\circ$ west of north.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Bearing of }L\\text{ from }P&=360^\\circ-15^\\circ\\\\\\text{Bearing of }L\\text{ from }P&=345^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 94
      }
    ]
